> Edit `templates/readme-snap_template` and run `python snapgen.py` to regenerate.

## How to build `snap` package

- Install `snapd`. [One](https://snapcraft.io/docs/installing-snapd) or [two](https://github.com/don-rumata/ansible-role-install-snap).

- Install `snapcraft`:

```bash
$ sudo snap install snapcraft --classic
```

- Update snapd:

```bash
$ sudo snap refresh snapcraft --edge
```

- Clone the repo:

```bash
$ git clone {{ release.website }}
```

- Change the directory:

```bash
$ cd ./jc
```

- Select branch:

```bash
$ git checkout {{ snap.branch }}
```

- Initialize LXD:

```bash
$ lxd init --auto
```

- Build `.snap` file:

```bash
$ snapcraft
```

## Snap configuration

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Base | `{{ snap.base }}` |
| Confinement | `{{ snap.confinement }}` |
| Grade | `{{ snap.grade }}` |
| Branch | `{{ snap.branch }}` |
| License | `{{ release.license }}` |

These values are read from `jc/lib.py` → `__release__['snap']` during
`snapcraft` build via the `override-pull` scriptlet.

## How to install local snap file

```bash
$ snap install --dangerous ./jc_*_amd64.snap
```

## How to use `jc` with plugins

- Put your plugin in the `"$HOME/.local/share/jc"` directory.

- To connect the directory, run:

```bash
snap connect jc:dot-jc-plugins snapd
```

